In short: the device plugin says "you're allowed to use RDMA," the Multus annotation says "here are the actual wires, with addresses, you can use it on." Drop the annotation and ibv_devinfo may still list devices as verbs objects, but NCCL has no routable GID/IP to establish a queue pair with a remote peer — which is exactly the failure mode we hit earlier this engagement (the launcher pod, which intentionally has no RDMA NIC attachments, trying to open mlx5_0 directly and failing).



